{
  "gate": "G0 (combined)",
  "verdict": "PASS",
  "decision": "Use the J-lens arm in Phase 2, offset 0, layers 9-26 only.",
  "why_the_frobenius_test_alone_was_misleading": "||J_l - I||/||I|| at the last source layer is 0.5787, which exactly reproduces the artifact's own reported final_identity_distance (0.578094), so the file is intact. But that residual is diffuse off-diagonal mass (RMS 0.0094 per entry over 3584^2 entries), not a scale error: best_scale_a = 0.999 and the mean diagonal rises monotonically 0.080 -> 0.999 across depth. Frobenius distance also cannot distinguish indexing conventions, so it is the wrong instrument for the offset question G0 actually asks.",
  "empirical_test": "J_l is defined as E[d h_final / d h_l], so the operational check is whether J_l . h_l predicts the true pre-norm final residual better than h_l does. Measured on 24 wikitext-like prose prompts, excluding positions 0-2 (Qwen2.5's attention sink is index 2).",
  "mean_cosine_gain_over_identity_layers_9_26": {
    "offset_0": 0.30757293877778236,
    "offset_1": 0.3055870267196938
  },
  "chosen_offset": 0,
  "offset_margin_is_not_meaningful": "offset 0 beats offset 1 by 0.0020 mean cosine. That is far too small to determine the convention. The honest statement is that the two are empirically equivalent on this model -- adjacent-layer Jacobians are near-identical -- so Phase 2's conclusions do not depend on the choice. Both offsets will be run as a robustness check.",
  "interpretable_window": {
    "layers": "9-26",
    "reason": "gains are negative or erratic at layers 1-5 and 7 and become reliably positive from layer 9. Matches the paper's own caveat that roughly the first third of the model is noisy and largely uninterpretable. Layer 27 has no J key (source_layers = 0..26, model has 28 layers)."
  },
  "licenses": "Using the J-lens on this base model with a stated indexing convention and a stated interpretable window.",
  "does_not_license": "Assuming the lens transfers to ORGANISM weights. J was fit on Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct, not on organisms A or B. dW is ~6% of base by relative Frobenius norm so the approximation is defensible, but it is an approximation and goes in the limitations regardless of outcome.",
